From w.huber@dkfz-heidelberg.de  Thu Dec 19 17:19:02 2002
From: w.huber@dkfz-heidelberg.de (Wolfgang Huber)
Date: Thu, 19 Dec 2002 18:19:02 +0100
Subject: [BioC] vsn / rma
In-Reply-To: <000001c2a776$519405b0$3f2d4381@DCYX8F0J>
Message-ID: <AGEOLPCFGCEABFJOOAAMMELHCBAA.w.huber@dkfz-heidelberg.de>

Hi Tom,

>How does the vsn method compare to rma, in terms of bias and the
>variance between replicates? Has anyone applied both methods to a
>standard dataset and compared the results?

I am not aware of a comprehensive comparison to RMA yet; However: vsn only
addresses the aspects "calibration" and "data transformation". The method
does not make recommendations on whether to use PM values only or to
subtract PM-MM, and on how to calculate the probe set average from the 16 or
20 values for the individual probes. Whereas RMA, as far as I am aware of,
does make such recommendations.

According to previous postings on this list, Oliver Hartmann is currently
working on a comparison on the test data set at
http://www.affymetrix.com/analysis/download_center2.affx. I will be highly
interested in the results of such comparisons!

Best regards
Wolfgang


